spec:
  grid: 23x28, background black
  sprite:
    count: exactly 1 foreground monochromatic 8-connected component
    color: orange (7)
    width: 3 [observed]
    height: 3 or 5 [observed]
    symmetry: LR and UD [observed]
    bbox: tight (sprite touches all 4 edges of its bbox)
    connectivity: single 8-connected component
    position: upper-left corner (r0, c0) with r0 in 4-7, c0 in 2-5
  slot_layout:
    h_spacing: sprite_width + 1 cols apart, starting at c0
    v_spacing: sprite_height + 1 rows apart, starting at r0
    h_slots: >=6 (enough for at least 2 pink columns, col_slot % 3 == 2)
    v_slots: >=3 (enough for vertical pink repetition to be visible)
  output:
    row_slot 0: all h_slots filled with sprite; col_slot%3 in {0,1} keep orange, col_slot%3==2 become pink (6)
    row_slot >0: only col_slot%3==2 slots filled, always pink
    copies clipped at grid edges

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct (input is simple; constraints are easy to satisfy constructively)
  steps:
    1. Grid is fixed 23x28 black.
    2. Design a small monochromatic sprite mask (3 wide, 3-5 tall) that is 8-connected, LR-symmetric, UD-symmetric, and touches all bbox edges.
    3. Pick (r0, c0) such that h_slots = floor((28 - c0) / (w+1)) + 1 >= 6 and v_slots = floor((23 - r0) / (h+1)) + 1 >= 3. For w=3 this means c0 <= 5; for h=3 means r0 <= 11, for h=5 means r0 <= 11.
    4. Stamp the orange sprite at (r0, c0) on the black grid. Input contains only this one sprite.
